h2. Summary

The compliance-operator successfully parses compliance framework references (NIST-800-53, CIS, PCI-DSS, BSI) from XCCDF data streams into Kubernetes Rule annotations. However, STIG-specific references are *completely missing* even though they exist in the source XCCDF files.

*Missing STIG Reference Types:*
# *SRG IDs* (Security Requirements Guide) - e.g., {{SRG-APP-000429-CTR-001060}}
# *STIG IDs* - e.g., {{CNTR-OS-000780}}
# *STIG Rule IDs* - e.g., {{SV-257564r1050650_rule}}
# *CCI IDs* (Control Correlation Identifiers) - e.g., {{CCI-000048}}

h2. Root Cause

*ComplianceAsCode PR #13793* (https://github.com/ComplianceAsCode/content/pull/13793) changed all STIG reference URLs from {{public.cyber.mil}} to {{www.cyber.mil}} to align with the official DISA domain.

The compliance-operator's {{referenceParser}} in {{pkg/profileparser/profileparser.go}} (line 872) was never updated:

\{code:java}
// Still looking for OLD domain
stigperr := p.registerStandard("STIG", `^https://public\.cyber\.mil/stigs/downloads/\?_dl_facet_stigs=container-platform`)
\{code}

*Timeline:*
* PR #13793 merged: August 14, 2025 (commit bce93f1caa)
* Affected: {{controls/stig_ocp4.yml}}, {{controls/stig_rhel9.yml}}, {{products/ocp4/product.yml}}, and more

h2. Steps to Reproduce

# Deploy compliance-operator with content built after August 14, 2025
# Check Rule annotations:
\{code}
oc get rule.compliance.openshift.io ocp4-api-server-encryption-provider-cipher \
  -n openshift-compliance -o yaml | grep 'control.compliance.openshift.io/'
\{code}
*Expected:* Annotations for SRG, STIGID, STIG-RULE
*Actual:* Only NIST-800-53, CIS-OCP, PCI-DSS, BSI

h2. Impact

* *Users cannot filter rules by STIG identifiers* - no way to find which rule implements CNTR-OS-000780
* *STIG compliance reporting is broken* - cannot map scan results to STIG requirements
* *Cross-framework mapping doesn't work* - must manually look up XCCDF
* *Affects all STIG products*: OCP4, RHEL9, OL9, Ubuntu 24.04, SUSE SLMICRO5, RHCOS4

h2. Proposed Solution

Update {{pkg/profileparser/profileparser.go}} to register all four STIG reference types with support for both domains:

\{code:java}
// SRG references (matches all facet types)
srgperr := p.registerStandard("SRG", `^https://(www|public)\.cyber\.mil/stigs/downloads/\?_dl_facet_stigs=`)
if srgperr != nil {
    log.Error(srgperr, "Could not register SRG reference parser")
}

// STIG IDs (CNTR-OS-* format)
stigidperr := p.registerStandard("STIGID", `^https://(www|public)\.cyber\.mil/stigs/downloads/\?_dl_facet_stigs=container-platform$`)
if stigidperr != nil {
    log.Error(stigidperr, "Could not register STIGID reference parser")
}

// STIG Rule IDs (SV-* format)
stigruleperr := p.registerStandard("STIG-RULE", `^https://(www|public)\.cyber\.mil/stigs/srg-stig-tools/$`)
if stigruleperr != nil {
    log.Error(stigruleperr, "Could not register STIG-RULE reference parser")
}

// CCI IDs
cciperr := p.registerStandard("CCI", `^https://(www|public)\.cyber\.mil/stigs/cci/$`)
if cciperr != nil {
    log.Error(cciperr, "Could not register CCI reference parser")
}
\{code}

*Expected annotations:*
* {{control.compliance.openshift.io/SRG: "SRG-APP-000429-CTR-001060;..."}}
* {{control.compliance.openshift.io/STIGID: "CNTR-OS-000780;..."}}
* {{control.compliance.openshift.io/STIG-RULE: "SV-257564r1050650_rule;..."}}
* {{control.compliance.openshift.io/CCI: "CCI-000048;..."}}

h2. Testing Requirements

# Add unit tests in {{pkg/profileparser/profileparser_test.go}} for all STIG annotation types
# Test with both {{www.cyber.mil}} and {{public.cyber.mil}} URLs (backward compatibility)
# Update test data to include {{www.cyber.mil}} STIG references
# Integration test on live cluster
# Verify no regression in existing parsers (NIST, CIS, PCI-DSS, BSI)

h2. Related Issues

*Upstream PR:* https://github.com/ComplianceAsCode/content/pull/13793
* Merged: August 14, 2025
* Author: Mab879
* Purpose: Align with official DISA domain (www.cyber.mil)

